{"duration": 50.943, "exact_word_timing": true, "lines": [{"beat": 0, "text": "A physician thrust his palm into a beating pigeon\u2019s chest.", "start": 0.08, "end": 3.189}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Colleagues laughed, calling his claim \u201ca wild fantasy.\u201d", "start": 3.609, "end": 6.467}, {"beat": 1, "text": "They clung to Galen\u2019s ancient idea that the liver spewed fresh blood.", "start": 6.687, "end": 10.301}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Harvey publishes De Motu Cordis in Frankfurt.", "start": 10.721, "end": 13.408}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Patients stop coming; his practice \u201cfalls mightily.\u201d", "start": 13.628, "end": 16.447}, {"beat": 3, "text": "You see, it\u2019s like watching a bathtub drain while the faucet keeps running \u2013 the water never disappears.", "start": 16.867, "end": 21.946}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Harvey measured the heart\u2019s capacity, counted beats, and proved the volume of blood moved each half\u2011hour was far too great for the liver to produce.", "start": 22.366, "end": 30.262}, {"beat": 4, "text": "His experiments on fish and serpents showed veins have one\u2011way valves, forcing blood to travel in a closed loop.", "start": 30.482, "end": 36.904}, {"beat": 5, "text": "The real reason he was mocked? He dared to replace a millennia\u2011old liver theory with a simple circular pump.", "start": 37.324, "end": 43.391}, {"beat": 6, "text": "Ironically, the same \u201ccirculation\u201d he proved later powered the very Royalist court that would exile him.", "start": 43.811, "end": 49.823}], "words": [{"w": "A", "start": 0.145, "end": 0.195, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "physician", "start": 0.245, "end": 0.745, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "thrust", "start": 0.845, "end": 1.095, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "his", "start": 1.12, "end": 1.245, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "palm", "start": 1.295, "end": 1.695, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "into", "start": 1.72, "end": 1.895, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "a", "start": 1.92, "end": 1.945,